.TH BACAK-DISPLAY-MANAGER 8 "June 2026" "BDM 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bacak-display-manager \- Bacak Desktop Wayland display manager daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bacak-display-manager
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bacak-display-manager
is the privileged core of the Bacak Display Manager (BDM). It is started by
systemd before user login, claims a virtual terminal, reads its configuration,
and either performs an automatic login or launches the unprivileged greeter
.BR bacak-greeter (1)
on the Bacak compositor.
.PP
The daemon drives PAM authentication on the greeter's behalf over a local UNIX
socket, then forks, drops privileges to the authenticated user, and hands off to
.BR bacak-session-launcher (8)
to start the chosen desktop session. It is the only BDM component that runs as
root.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I /etc/bacak-display-manager.conf
Main configuration (TOML). See the file's comments for all keys: autologin,
greeter, theme, wallpaper, virtual keyboard, accessibility, power and sessions.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/bacak-display-manager
PAM policy for interactive logins.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/bacak-autologin
PAM policy for the autologin fast-path.
.TP
.I /run/bacak-display-manager/greeter.sock
Greeter IPC socket (root-owned, greeter-group readable).
.TP
.I /var/lib/bacak-display-manager/
Persisted last-user / last-session state.
.SH SERVICE
Managed via systemd:
.PP
.RS
systemctl enable --now bacak-display-manager
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bacak-greeter (1),
.BR bacak-session-launcher (8),
.BR systemd-logind.service (8),
.BR pam (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Bacak Desktop Project.
